This example's network is derived from Ultralytics YOLOv8 and carries
AGPL-3.0. Distributing a device or a service built on it places
obligations on the whole product, which is not true of the other network
examples here. The firmware also contains STMicroelectronics software
under SLA0044, whose terms in most cases forbid distributing, or using
other than internally, software that combines the two while AGPL-3.0
governs the model.

This example's main.c is licensed under AGPL-3.0 as well, as it embeds
the network; the licence text is
Middlewares/NeuroN6/Models/YoloV8Pose/LICENSE.AGPL-3.0.txt.

Because this file is present, harness/compile.sh and
harness/examples/cubebuild.sh --all skip this example, and a default build
of this repository produces nothing derived from that network. To build it
anyway:

    NEURON6_BUILD_RESTRICTED=1 bash harness/compile.sh
    bash harness/examples/cubebuild.sh Camera_YoloV8Pose_WiFi_FreeRTOS

See this example's README, and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, before showing,
shipping or handing over anything built from it.
